Evaluator: A. Psaltis (04/2025)
Comments:
1. Resonances with measured strengths: Er= 560, 875, 1110 and 1155 keV. For Er= 560 keV we are using the strength of Hardie et al. (1984).
For the Er= 876 keV we use a Bayesian weighted average between the measurements by Hardie et al. (1984) and Psaltis et al. (2022).
For Er= 1110 and 1155 keV we are using the strengths of Psaltis et al. (2022).
2. For the subthreshold resonance at Er= -44 keV we are using the prescription of Hartos et al. (2018)
For the theta^2 we are using a reduced alpha width of 0.1 with a factor of 5 uncertainty.
3. For the resonances with Er>1500 keV, G_a and G_p values are taken from Freer et al. (2012).
G_g are taken as being 1eV with a factor of 10 uncertainty, except for the 2101 keV, where the G_g is taken from the mirror.
5. The direct capture (DC) is adopted from the work of Hartos et al. (2018).
